{
 "id": "accounting-comparison",
 "title": "How much of world energy is solar and wind? Two answers",
 "description": "The same two technologies, the same years, the same publisher \u2014 differing by a factor of about 2.4 depending only on whether renewable electricity is counted at face value or scaled up to the fossil fuel it displaces. Most figures quoted in public are one of these without saying which.",
 "group": "sources",
 "sources": [
